p.src:
Light gives the shortest version of the same calculation. For a radial null ray, $d\tau^2
=a\,dt^2-\frac{dr^2}{a}=0.$ Therefore $\boxed{
\frac{dr}{dt}
=\pm a(r)
=\pm\left(1-\frac{r_s}{r}\right).
}$ The plus sign describes an outgoing ray and the minus sign an ingoing ray. Both coordinate speeds tend to zero at the horizon.

